# councillormosley — Councillor Mosley's entire conversation, every quest he appears in.
#
# A quests/dialogue/ file: DIALOGUE blocks and NO QUEST block. The importer and
# Tools -> Content -> Validate Quests both refuse either mistake. See
# docs/reference/QUEST_TEXT_FORMAT.md.
#
# ⚠ THIS FILE OWNS COUNCILLOR MOSLEY'S CONVERSATION. One DIALOGUE block per npcId across the
# whole quests/ tree: each import regenerates Dialogue_councillormosley.asset wholesale, so a
# second file declaring DIALOGUE councillormosley would clobber this one. Every future Mosley
# quest adds its nodes HERE, gated on its own quest id.
#
# The quests whose beats live in this file:
#   mosley_vape_quest_one  - quests/mosley_vape_quest_one.quest  (granted and completed here)
#   daniel_pauls_quest_one - quests/daniel_pauls_quest_one.quest (granted here at nag_two;
#                            completed in quests/dialogue/danielpauls.quest)
#   wtf_mosley             - quests/wtf_mosley.quest             (completed here; granted by Daniel's
#                            Quest 4 report, quests/dialogue/danielpauls.quest node dbb_chat)
#
# All of Councillor Mosley's player lines are the owner's own words, written in on 2026-08-15. No
# [TODO: ] blanks remain in this file.

DIALOGUE councillormosley
# councillormosley matches Preset_CouncillorMosley's filename (Preset_ prefix stripped,
# case-insensitive) — the importer wires this conversation into that preset's Conversation
# field automatically.

NODE start
SPEAKER: councillormosley
SPEAK: Yes? What is it, chap? I'm under an immense amount of stress here.
CHOICE Are you alright? You look like you've seen a ghost. -> intro_panic
GATE: not-started mosley_vape_quest_one
CHOICE About that vape situation in the basement... -> nag_one
GATE: active mosley_vape_quest_one
# wtf_mosley branch. Mosley greets first ("Ey up, lad.").
CHOICE Right, Mosley! We need to talk about where those vapes came from. -> wm_greet
GATE: active wtf_mosley
CHOICE How are things holding up with the council? -> idle_council
GATE: complete wtf_mosley
CHOICE Just passing by.

NODE intro_panic
SPEAKER: councillormosley
SPEAK: Christ... what have I done? You! No... no, please, leave me be!
CHOICE Come on, what's up? Caught with the intern again? -> reveal_prompt
CHOICE Suit yourself.

NODE reveal_prompt
SPEAKER: councillormosley
SPEAK: Agh! I don't have time to care if you leak this to the press. You've probably noticed an uptick in... undesirable behaviour around here?
CHOICE You mean the nitties losing their minds? -> reveal_a
CHOICE Can you just spit it out? -> reveal_b

NODE reveal_a
SPEAKER: councillormosley
SPEAK: YES! Well, no... they're just misunderstood constituents. Anyway, I tried to calm them down. I asked ChatJeeves LLM, and three hours later I had a prototype calming vape. I was told it would pacify the oiks, but bloody hell old boy, they've gone completely feral!
CHOICE Right, and why are you telling me this? -> ask_why_1
CHOICE Sounds tasty. A toot for me perchance, old boy? -> ask_why_2

NODE reveal_b
SPEAKER: councillormosley
SPEAK: Right, fine. Had a consult with an AI assistant, whipped up a prototype chill-out vape, and tested it on a few local ruffians.
CHOICE Right, and why are you telling me this? -> ask_why_1
CHOICE Sounds tasty. A toot for me perchance, old boy? -> ask_why_2

NODE ask_why_1
SPEAKER: councillormosley
SPEAK: I've spoken to Daniel Pauls — I know you've got magical capabilities. I'll report you to the Old Bill if you don't help me clean this up! Help me recover the prototype and there's a handsome sum in it for you. Please! *eyes begin to tear up*
CHOICE Well, since you asked nicely... go on then. -> end_accept
GRANT: mosley_vape_quest_one
CHOICE Bugger off. -> end_decline

NODE ask_why_2
SPEAKER: councillormosley
SPEAK: They're bloody rabid, you fool! I'll tell you where they are, just fetch back that vape! If word gets out, it's Black Mamba 2.0 and this place becomes Manchester!
CHOICE Right, maybe not then. What exactly do you need done? -> ask_why_1
CHOICE I'm out.

NODE end_accept
SPEAKER: councillormosley
SPEAK: Splendid! I've marked the cellar details in your journal. I'll be right here waiting. Chop chop, old boy!

NODE end_decline
SPEAKER: councillormosley
SPEAK: Agh! I'll be right here weeping if you change your mind!

NODE nag_one
SPEAKER: councillormosley
SPEAK: COME ON CHAP! GET ME THAT VAPE AND DO NOT TAKE A PUFF ON IT!
CHOICE Keep your hair on, I'm working on it. -> nag_two

NODE nag_two
SPEAKER: councillormosley
SPEAK: WHAT ARE YOU WAITING FOR?! I CAN PRACTICALLY HEAR THEM HUFFING IT FROM HERE!
CHOICE Here's your vape. What did you put in this, chemical weapons? -> vape_returned
ITEM: cherry_mango_vape x1 consume
COMPLETE: mosley_vape_quest_one
GRANT: daniel_pauls_quest_one
CHOICE Just give me a bit more time.

NODE vape_returned
SPEAKER: councillormosley
SPEAK: Good man! Splendid work. Now, you should get back over to Daniel Pauls — I hear he's in a spot of bother near the church.
CHOICE On my way.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# wtf_mosley - "WTF Mosley?" (Quest 5).
#
# Reached from NODE start's  GATE: active wtf_mosley  choice. One straight run of single-choice
# nodes: Mosley confesses, the player presses him on. The last choice has no  ->  , so it ends the
# conversation, and its COMPLETE: is what finishes the quest's single MANUAL stage.

NODE wm_greet
SPEAKER: councillormosley
SPEAK: Ey up, lad! How are we doing? Have you spoken to Daniel Pauls?
CHOICE Mosley... where did you actually get those vapes from? -> wm_made

NODE wm_made
SPEAKER: councillormosley
SPEAK: I made them! I asked the AI engine, sourced the components myself. Why do you ask?
CHOICE Scrap Man saw you buying a crate of Chinese-stamped vapes from Ralph and Sanjeet. -> wm_thing

NODE wm_thing
SPEAKER: councillormosley
SPEAK: No... well, you see... the nuance of the situation is...
CHOICE Out with it, Mosley. -> wm_toomuch

NODE wm_toomuch
SPEAKER: councillormosley
SPEAK: It was just too much, old boy! The borough's going down the tubes, the Neeks were rioting, and I didn't know what else to do!
CHOICE Go on. -> wm_experiment

NODE wm_experiment
SPEAKER: councillormosley
SPEAK: I read online that overseas authorities use sedating vapours for crowd pacification. The council would never approve the budget, so I used my personal allowance! It was purely an off-the-books civic trial!
CHOICE But Mosley, you bought them off street gangs. Why? -> wm_korean

NODE wm_korean
SPEAKER: councillormosley
SPEAK: Well, they assured me it was high-grade Korean import! I questioned the labels, but Sanjeet told me not to be culturally insensitive. Who was I to argue?
CHOICE Sanjeet is from Birmingham, Mosley. He's not an East Asian import authority. -> wm_same

NODE wm_same
SPEAKER: councillormosley
SPEAK: Well, it's all rather exotic to me, isn't it? Bit of this, bit of that...
CHOICE Right, let's stop before you dig a deeper hole. Where are Ralph and Sanjeet holing up? -> wm_where

NODE wm_where
SPEAKER: councillormosley
SPEAK: They operate out of a trap house near the abandoned bus station up north. That's where we concluded our transaction.
# Completes Quest 5 and grants Quest 6 from one choice — the same shape as dpq1_speed and dbb_chat.
# Mosley's line above is already the location brief for the raid, so the hand-off needed no new
# prose: "a little place near the abandoned bus station" IS the trap house.
CHOICE I'll pay them a visit. Try to stay out of trouble, Councillor.
COMPLETE: wtf_mosley
GRANT: gangbusters

NODE idle_council
SPEAKER: councillormosley
SPEAK: I'm keeping a low profile, old boy. If the Standards Committee catches wind of any of this, I'll be managing bins in Croydon.
CHOICE Probably for the best.
